WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.880
Montessori Education is based on the principles developed by Maria Montessori,

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:11.460
who opened her first school for children of low-income workers in an apartment building in Rome in 1907.

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:15.800
The school was called 
“Casa dei Bambini”, Home for Children.

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:20.440
This first “Casa” was furnished with a teachers table,

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:24.820
a stove, a blackboard, some chairs,
group tables for the children

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:29.320
and a cabinet filled with materials
that Montessori developed in her earlier career

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:34.780
when she researched how to teach kids who experience some form of mental disability.

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:38.640
Maria Montessori created the materials 
after she realised

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:45.200
that students seem to understand complex concepts better when they engaged all their senses.

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:51.940
Activities at this first school included personal care (such as dressing and undressing),

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:55.500
care of the environment like sweeping,
dusting and gardening.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:58.980
Otherwise they were free to move around 
and play with the materials.

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:01.400
Montessori did not teach herself

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:05.400
but instead oversaw the classroom work
of her teachers.

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:11.300
Montessori observed that children showed
episodes of deep concentration

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:14.140
and multiple repetitions of the same activity.

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:15.700
Given free choice,

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:19.420
kids showed more interest in practical activities 
and the materials

00:01:19.420 --> 00:01:22.400
than normal toys, sweets or other rewards.

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:26.160
Over time spontaneous self-discipline emerged.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:30.820
Montessori concluded that working independently

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:35.680
children seemed to reach new levels of autonomy and become self-motivated learners.

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:39.820
She began to see the role of the teacher as a facilitator of young human beings

00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:44.280
who are free to move and act within the limits of a prepared environment.

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:52.000
The goal: to grow children to become independent and responsible adults who share a love for learning.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:58.000
Soon after Montessori herself and her ideas
started travelling the world

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:01.900
to inspired progressive thinkers and educators
from all over.

00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:06.980
The inventors, Alexander Graham Bell and Thomas Edison, became early advocates.

00:02:06.980 --> 00:02:10.280
Later alumni include Jimmy Wales from Wikipedia,

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:12.620
author Gabriel Garcia Marquez

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:17.280
as well as the two Google founders Larry Page and Sergey Brin.

00:02:18.460 --> 00:02:23.420
Today the term “Montessori” stands more for a method, than a school itself.

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:28.940
The fact that it can be used freely by anyone led to a great variation of schools.

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:32.820
Educators all over the world borrow Montessori's name,

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:36.320
insights and materials to organize kindergartens,

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:39.040
elementary schools, special needs programs,

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:41.580
or even full 12 year curriculums.

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:44.320
Some parents use it for homeschooling.

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:49.100
The following characteristics are shared 
among most programs:

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:51.840
- Students are free to choose what to learn

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:54.980
- Open classrooms that allow free movement

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:58.460
- Use of specialised Montessori materials

00:02:58.660 --> 00:03:03.720
- Mixed age classes (from 0-3, 3-6 or 6-12)

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:06.060
so children can learn from each other

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:10.220
- Uninterrupted blocks of study time, usually three hours

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:12.160
- No grading or homework

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:14.380
- and a trained teacher

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:18.920
Maria Montessori once famously said:

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:23.540
“Never help a child with a task 
at which he feels he can succeed.”

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:25.940
What are your thoughts on Montessori?

00:03:25.940 --> 00:03:29.300
Please share your opinions in the comments below!

